  "question": {
    "html": "<p>In a photoelectric experiment a stopping voltage <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span> required to prevent photoelectrons from flowing across the photoelectric cell is measured for light of two frequencies <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{1}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{2}\"></span>. The results obtained are shown.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The ratio <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{V_{2}-V_{1}}{f_{2}-f_{1}}\"></span> is an estimate of</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"e\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"h\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{e}{h}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{h}{e}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
